    "freeTraits": 0,
    "biography": "<h2>Background</h2><p>A modernist Ventrue and childe of Hardestadt the Younger, Jan Pieterzoon dismisses Gehenna and the Book of Nod as superstitious paranoia that breeds factionalism and paralysis within the Camarilla, and believes the sect must embrace change and adapt to the new millennium or risk a self-fulfilling collapse born of its own fear. He has acquired significant media influence, which he directs toward a quiet crusade to suppress references to the Book of Nod and to fund 'scientific' explanations for vampirism that might quell the apocalyptic dread spreading through Kindred society.</p><h2>Roleplaying Hints</h2><p>Despite his skepticism of Kindred superstition and prophecy, Jan genuinely upholds Ventrue noblesse oblige, believing the clan's true duty is to guide &mdash; not merely dominate &mdash; the rest of Kindred society. Play him as pragmatic, forward-looking, and quietly contemptuous of elders who let fear of Gehenna paralyze their decision-making; he is a reformer within the Camarilla, not against it.</p><p><strong>Disciplines (as printed, dot-rating, convert to owned Discipline Items at Storyteller discretion):</strong> Auspex 1, Dominate 4, Fortitude 5, Obfuscate 2, Obtenebration 1, Potence 3, Presence 4.</p>",
    "notes": "Sire: Hardestadt the Younger. Embrace: 1723. Clanbook: Ventrue, Chapter Three (The Revered Caste).",
